          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong monoidal category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            equipped with some notion of ‘tensor product’ of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} traditional tensor product
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon V \to W
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\prime \colon V^\prime \to W^\prime
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \otimes f^\prime \colon V \otimes V^\prime \to W \otimes W^\prime \,.
          %p
            The same category can often be made into a monoidal category in more than one way. For example the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            can be made into a monoidal category with cartesian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            (i.e.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            into a monoidal category with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            as the ‘tensor product’ — this may seem perverse, but it’s actually very useful.
          %p
            For any monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          #eq:TensorProductFunctor.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi M
                  %mo ×
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\otimes \colon  M \times M \longrightarrow M
          %p
            This functor, which we can think of as a kind of ‘multiplication’, makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} vertically categorified
            version of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
          %p
            A monoidal category can also be considered a one-object
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#DefinitionGeneralMonoidalCategories General monoidal categories
