                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
            %li#Borceux94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Section 6.1 of:
                %em Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                Vol. 2:
                %em Categories and Structures
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525865"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525865
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 50
            %li#EGNO15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"}> Pavel Etingof
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shlomo+Gelaki"} Shlomo Gelaki
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Nikshych"} Dmitri Nikshych
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ostrik"} Victor Ostrik
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tensor Categories
                %strong 205
                (2015) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-205"}> ISBN:978-1-4704-3441-0
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www-math.mit.edu/~etingof/egnobookfinal.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
            %li#Perrone24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"}> Paolo Perrone
                , Chapter 6 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Starting Category Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/13670"} doi:10.1142/13670
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1912.10642"} arXiv:1912.10642
          %p
            Exposition of basics of monoidal categories and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} geometry of physics – categories and toposes
              , Section 2:
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#BasicNotionsOfCategoricalAlgebra"} Basic notions of categorical algebra
          %p History:
          %p
            A version of monoidal categories were introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"} Jean Bénabou
            under the name ‘categorie avec multiplication’. However, he gave the coherence laws incorrectly, by stating that all diagrams of a certain form commute, when in fact not all these diagrams need commute. Mac Lane’s 1963 paper was the first to give a correct (and finite) axiomatisation, under the name ‘bicategory’ (not to be confused with the contemporary meaning of
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
                ,
                %em Catégories avec multiplication
                , C. R. Acad. Sci. Paris
                %strong 256
                (1963) 1887-1890 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k3208j/f1965.image"}> gallica
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
                ,
                %em Algèbre élémentaire dans les catégories avec multiplication
                , C. R. Acad. Sci. Paris
                %strong 258
                (1964) 771-774 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k40102/f817.image"}> gallica
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#MacLane
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"}> Saunders Mac Lane
                ,
                %em Natural Associativity and Commutativity
                , Rice University Studies
                %strong 49
                (1963) pp.28-46.
          %p Shortly after Mac Lane’s definition appeared, Max Kelly showed how the coherence axioms could be whittled down to just two:
          %ul
            %li#Kelly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On MacLane’s Conditions for Coherence of Natural Associativities, Commutativities, etc.
              %strong 1
              (1964) pp.397-402.
          %p For a quick history of monoidal categories including an explanation of why Benabou’s definition is incorrect, see Section 2 here:
          %ul
            %li#BaezSinh
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hoàng Xuân Sính’s Thesis: Categorifying Group Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.05119"} arXiv
          %p
            Lecture notes on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            of monoidal categories:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"}> Pavel Etingof
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shlomo+Gelaki"} Shlomo Gelaki
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Nikshych"} Dmitri Nikshych
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ostrik"} Victor Ostrik
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topics in Lie theory and Tensor categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mathematics/18-769-topics-in-lie-theory-tensor-categories-spring-2009/lecture-notes/"} web
          %p
            A brief discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Basic concepts of enriched category theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 64
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10abs.html"} tac
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10.pdf"} pdf
          %p A survey of some applications is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monoidal categories in, and linking, geometry and algebra
              %strong 19
              5 (2012) 769-820 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.2991"}> arXiv:1201.2991
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/bulletin-of-the-belgian-mathematical-society-simon-stevin/volume-19/issue-5/Monoidal-categories-in-and-linking-geometry-and-algebra/10.36045/bbms/1354031551.full"} doi:10.36045/bbms/1354031551
          %p
            (for more see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fusion+category"} fusion category
            etc.).
          %p Quick surveys of relevant definitions include also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                John Armstrong,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://unapologetic.wordpress.com/2007/06/28/monoidal-categories/"} Monoidal categories
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monoidal_category"}> Monoidal category
                  \.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/qg-fall2004/definitions.pdf"} Some definitions everyone should know
          %p
            For an elementary introduction to monoidal categories using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Stay"} Mike Stay
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/rosetta.pdf"} Physics, topology, logic and computation: a Rosetta Stone
              = succeed "," do
                %em New Structures for Physics
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bob+Coecke"} Bob Coecke
          %p
            A more detailed tour of monoidal categories, also using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Selinger"}> Peter Selinger
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathstat.dal.ca/~selinger/papers.html#graphical"} A survey of graphical languages for monoidal categories
          %p
            Textbook account with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+quantum+mechanics+in+terms+of+dagger-compact+categories"} finite quantum mechanics in terms of dagger-compact categories
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
          %ul
            %li#HeunenVicary19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jamie+Vicary"} Jamie Vicary
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categories for Quantum Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/categories-for-quantum-theory-9780198739616"} ISBN:9780198739616
          %p Concerning the scalars:
          %ul
            %li#KellyLaplaza80
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+L.+Laplaza"} M. L. Laplaza
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Coherence for compact closed categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049%2880%2990101-2"} 10.1016/0022-4049(80)90101-2
            %li#AbramskyCoecke04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samson+Abramsky"}> Samson Abramsky
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bob+Coecke"} Bob Coecke
                %em A categorical semantics of quantum protocols
                , Proceedings of the 19th IEEE conference on Logic in Computer Science (LiCS’04). IEEE Computer Science Press (2004) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0402130"}> arXiv:quant-ph/0402130
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+categories"} univalent categories
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+foundations+of+mathematics"} univalent foundations of mathematics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            with the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kobe+Wullaert"}> Kobe Wullaert
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Matthes"} Ralph Matthes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benedikt+Ahrens"} Benedikt Ahrens
              %em Univalent Monoidal Categories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03146"}> arXiv:2212.03146
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Some remarks on different monoidal structures on the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/punkdit/categories/blob/26b751bbcbe6765fe447e805629ff6416f4c38b1/gmane/science/mathematics/categories/4477"}> Set as a monoidal category
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+mailing+list"} categories mailing list
          %p On an alternative definition of monoidal category based on a different kind of unit:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Kock"}> Joachim Kock
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Elementary remarks on units in monoidal categories
          %p
            which is further discussed in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew-monoidal+categories"} skew-monoidal categories
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              Jim Andrianopoulos,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Remarks on units of skew monoidal categories
